{ You are Black. His queen stands in the middle, yours sits on e2 inside his camp, and his knight on b1 still has to come out. }
14. Nd2 { His knight comes out to d2, right beside your queen. That is the mistake: his c pawn had to move first. } 14... e5 { The pawn attacks his queen on d4. Every safe square she has leaves the knight on d2 without a guard. [%cal Ge5d4] } (14... Rd8 { A useful rook move, but it gives him time to chase your queen away from the knight. } 15. Bf3 Qa6 16. e4 e5 { His bishop on f3 chased your queen off e2, so the pawn push wins nothing. It is about level. [%csl Gd2] }) (14... Qh5 { The queen leaves e2 on her own, and the knight on d2 is no longer attacked. } 15. Nf3 Qg4 16. Qxg4 Nxg4 { The queens come off, the knight got away, and he is slightly better. [%csl Gf3] }) (14... Qg4 { This steps off e2, and nothing attacks the knight on d2 any more. } 15. f4 Bd7 16. Nf3 Rfd8 { His knight reached f3 safely, and he is slightly better. [%csl Gf3] }) (14... Qxd2 { You grab the knight at once, and his queen takes yours. [%cal Rd4d2] } 15. Qxd2 { Your queen went for a knight. He is winning. [%csl Rd2] }) (14... Qxf2+ { A check that simply gives up the queen: his rook takes her. [%cal Rf1f2] } 15. Rxf2 { A queen for a pawn. He is winning. [%csl Rf2] }) 15. Qxe5 { His queen takes the pawn on e5. From there she no longer guards the knight on d2. } 15... Qxd2 { A free knight on d2. Your pawn pulled his queen off her post: that is deflection. One pawn given, one knight taken. } (15... Re8 { Chasing his queen gives her time to come back. } 16. Qd4 Bf5 17. a5 Rac8 { His queen is back on d4 guarding the knight, you are a pawn down, and he is better. [%csl Rd2] }) (15... Bg4 { The bishop does nothing to his queen, and she walks back to d4. } 16. Qd4 Bf5 17. h3 Rfd8 { The knight on d2 is guarded again, and you are a pawn down. He is better. [%csl Rd2] }) (15... Qxf2+ { A check that hands him your queen for a pawn. [%cal Rf1f2] } 16. Rxf2 { A queen for a pawn: he is winning. [%csl Rf2] }) (15... d4 { The pawn attacks nothing that matters, and his queen takes it. } 16. Qxd4 { She is back on d4 guarding the knight, and you are two pawns down. He is much better. [%csl Rd4] }) 0-1


[Event "Intermediate tactics: the decoy, the lesson"]
