{ You are White, the exchange down, and his rook is heading for your back row. Without a trick you are losing. }
36... Qe6 { He offers the queens off, and that is the mistake: his king should have stepped back to g7. } 37. Qxe6+ { Queen takes queen with check. His king has to take back, or he is a whole queen down. [%csl Re6] } (37. Qd3 { Your queen steps back, and his rook and queen keep their grip. } 37... Rc7 { You are still the exchange down with no trick left, and he is winning. [%csl Rc7] }) (37. Qb7+ { A check, but his king steps away and your queen has nothing to do. } 37... Kf6 { His king is safe and his rook is coming. He is winning. [%csl Rf6] }) (37. Bf3 { Your bishop goes to f3, and his queen takes yours. } 37... Qxd5 38. Bxd5+ { The queens are off and you are the exchange down. He is winning. [%csl Rd5] }) 37... Kxe6 { His king takes back on e6, out in the open. [%csl Re6] } 38. Bg4+ { Check along the diagonal, and behind his king on that diagonal sits his rook. Wherever the king steps, the rook falls. [%cal Gg4e6,Ge6c8] } (38. Bd3 { The bishop goes to the wrong diagonal, and his rook comes for your back row. } 38... Rc1+ { His rook is in, the exchange up. He is winning. [%csl Rc1] }) (38. Kg1 { A king move, and his rook comes for your pawns. } 38... Rc2 { His rook is on your second row, and he is winning. [%csl Rc2] }) (38. Bf3 { Your bishop goes to f3, and his rook comes in with check. } 38... Rc1+ 39. Kg2 Rc2+ { His rook checks and takes a pawn next. He is winning. [%csl Rc2] }) 38... Ke5 { His king steps off the diagonal, and his rook is left alone at the far end of it. } 39. Bxc8 { A whole rook. The queen trade dragged his king onto the diagonal of your bishop, right in front of his rook: that is the decoy. [%csl Gc8] } (39. b4 { A pawn move, and his rook comes in with check. } 39... Rc1+ 40. Kg2 Rc2+ { His rook checks and takes your pawns. He is winning. [%csl Rc2] }) (39. Kg1 { A king move, and his rook comes in with check. } 39... Rc1+ 40. Kg2 Rc2+ { His rook checks and goes pawn hunting. He is winning. [%csl Rc2] }) (39. Bd7 { Your bishop attacks the rook instead of taking it, and it runs with check. } 39... Rc1+ { The rook got out with check, and he is winning. [%csl Rc1] }) 1-0


