{ You are Black. His knight on d5 has jumped deep into your camp, and his queen on d4 stands behind it. Interference: find the line to cut. }
12. Nb6 { His knight jumps to b6 and attacks your rook in the corner, and that is the mistake: it belonged in the middle. His queen on d4 is its only guard. } 12... c5 { Your pawn steps to c5 and attacks his queen. It also stands on her diagonal to b6, cutting her off from the knight. [%cal Rd4b6] } (12... Ra7 { The rook dodges, but his knight on b6 stays guarded. } 13. Nd5 Rb7 14. Nf4 Qf6 { His knight got back out to f4, and he is better. [%csl Rf4] }) (12... Nd7 { This leaves your rook on a8 to the knight. } 13. Nxa8 Qxa8 14. Nxc4 d5 { You lost a rook for a knight and the c4 pawn. He is winning. [%csl Ra8] }) (12... d5 { The wrong pawn: it does not touch the line from d4 to b6. } 13. Nxa8 Nd7 14. O-O Qxa8 { You won his knight back, but he is the exchange up. [%csl Ra8] }) (12... Qxb6 { You take the knight, and his queen takes yours. [%cal Rd4b6] } 13. Qxb6 { His knight was guarded, and your queen is gone for it. He is winning. [%csl Rb6] }) (12... Bxh3 { A pawn, and his rook takes the bishop. [%cal Rh1h3] } 13. Rxh3 { A bishop for a pawn, and your rook is still attacked. He is winning. [%csl Rh3] }) 13. Qe3 { His queen steps back to e3. Your pawn still blocks her way to b6. } 13... Qxb6 { A free knight. Your pawn on c5 stood between his queen and b6: that is interference. } (13... Ra7 { The rook dodges, and his knight on b6 hops out with a pawn. } 14. Nbxc4 Nc6 15. Qg3 Nd4 { His knight escaped to c4, and he is slightly better. [%csl Rc4] }) (13... Nc6 { Your rook on a8 is still attacked, and his knight takes it. } 14. Nxa8 Nd4 15. Kd1 Be7 16. f4 Qxa8 { You took the knight in the corner at last, but a rook for a knight is a rook for a knight. He is better. [%csl Ra8] }) (13... c3 { The pawn runs on, but his knight escapes with your rook still attacked. } 14. Ndc4 Nd7 15. Nd5 { His knights are safe in the middle, and he is better. [%csl Rd5] }) (13... Be7 { Your rook is still attacked, and his knight takes it. } 14. Nxa8 { His knight took your rook, and you are a rook down for now. Catching the knight in the corner takes time. He is better. [%csl Ra8] }) 0-1


