{ You are White, two pawns down, but your rooks own the d column. His queen sits on b7. }
18... Be7 { His bishop drops back to e7, and that is the mistake: it was the queen that belonged there. } 19. Rd7 { Your rook lands on d7, between his queen and his bishop on e7, and it attacks the queen. [%cal Rb7e7] } (19. Bh6 { The bishop eyes g7, but his queen still guards e7 and he answers calmly. [%cal Rb7e7] } 19... Qb8 20. Bf4 Qe8 21. Qg4 f5 { He is still two pawns up and slightly better. [%csl Re7] }) (19. Qg3 { The queen looks active, but he has time to bring the bishop to f6. } 19... Bf6 20. Bg5 Bxg5 21. Qxg5 h6 { The bishops are off, you are still two pawns down, and he is better. [%csl Rh6] }) (19. Qxc6 { You grab a pawn, and his queen takes yours. [%cal Rb7c6] } 19... Qxc6 { She ate your queen for the price of a pawn. He is winning. [%csl Rc6] }) (19. Rd8 { Your rook goes to his back row, and his rook takes it. [%cal Ra8d8] } 19... Raxd8 { A whole rook gone, and you were already two pawns down. He is winning. [%csl Rd8] }) (19. Qxf7+ { A check that costs the queen: his rook takes her. [%cal Rf8f7] } 19... Rxf7 { His rook took your queen, and one pawn is all it cost him. He is winning. [%csl Rf7] }) 19... Qa6 { His queen runs to a6 and leaves the seventh row. } 20. Rxe7 { A free bishop. Your rook on d7 cut the row between his queen and e7: that is interference. You win back more than the two pawns. } (20. Bf4 { A calm move, and his bishop gets away. } 20... Rae8 21. h4 Qxa2 22. Be5 Qa5 { His rook on e8 guards the bishop, he took your a2 pawn, and it is about level. [%csl Ge8] }) (20. Qxc6 { One pawn instead of a whole bishop. } 20... Bf6 21. a3 Qa5 22. g3 Qxc3 { His bishop escaped, he took your c3 pawn back, and he is slightly better. [%csl Rc3] }) (20. a3 { A quiet pawn move, and his rook comes to guard the bishop. } 20... Rae8 21. h3 c5 { His bishop is guarded, he is still two pawns up, and he is better. [%csl Re8] }) (20. R7d6 { Your rook steps back onto a square his bishop attacks, and the bishop takes it. [%cal Re7d6] } 20... Bxd6 { A rook for nothing, and you were two pawns down already. He is winning. [%csl Rd6] }) 1-0


