{ You are Black, the exchange and two pawns down, and his queen has gone all the way into your corner. }
14. O-O { He castles, and that is the mistake: his queen should have stepped to a7 first. [%csl Ra8] } 14... Bb7 { Your bishop attacks his queen. Her only square is a7, and that one has a problem too. [%cal Gb7a8] } (14... h6 { A quiet move, and his queen slips out to d5. } 15. Qd5 { She is free, and with his extra material he is much better. [%csl Rd5] }) (14... Re8 { A rook move, and his queen slips out to d5. } 15. Qd5 { She is free and in the middle, and he is much better. [%csl Rd5] }) (14... Bf5 { The bishop goes the wrong way, and his queen escapes. } 15. Qd5 { She is free, and with the exchange and two pawns more he is winning. [%csl Rd5] }) 15. Qa7 { His queen steps to a7, the only square she had. Is she safe there? [%csl Ra7] } 15... Ra8 { Your rook attacks the queen. She can take your bishop, but then your knight takes her. [%cal Ga8a7] } (15... Bxf3 { You take the knight, and the chase is over. } 16. gxf3 Qg5+ 17. Kh1 Qf4 { His queen escaped, and with his extra material he is slightly better. [%csl Ra7] }) (15... Bd5 { The bishop steps back, and his pawn chases your knight. } 16. b4 { His queen is free again, and he is much better. [%csl Rb4] }) (15... Re8 { A rook move, and his pawn chases your knight. } 16. b4 { His queen escapes, and he is much better. [%csl Rb4] }) 16. Qxb7 { His queen takes your bishop, the only thing she could do. } 16... Nxb7 { Your knight takes his queen. She was cornered and had no safe square: that is the trapped piece. A queen for a bishop. [%csl Gb7] } (16... Rd8 { You leave his queen alive on b7. } 17. Qb4 { She escaped, and he is winning. [%csl Rb4] }) (16... Qxe5 { You grab a pawn, and his queen takes your rook with check. [%cal Rb7a8] } 17. Qxa8+ { Your rook is gone, and mate follows. You are lost. [%csl Ra8] }) 0-1
